{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310872,"nonce":"8Oh9Qkz+6F7rKoSJl60UEJ30d7U=","title":"Phased plan for WebAssembly backend + async/await in WASM","message":"**Why:** Universal compilation target — one .wasm runs in browsers, WASI, edge workers. Component Model for universal rpkg packages.\n\n\n`compiler/src/codegen/wasm_backend.rs` (~2000 lines). MIR → WASM via wasm-encoder. Full instruction lowering, br_table dispatch for CFG, phi resolution, shadow stack, string pool. Producer-based type inference pass for float correctness. `rayzor build --target wasm` CLI.\n\n`runtime-wasm/src/lib.rs` (~2000 lines). 106+ exports: strings, math, arrays, box/unbox, type system, anonymous objects. Compiles to wasm32-wasip1 (52KB). Linked into user module by `wasm_linker.rs` (1965 lines).\n\nFile I/O via `std::fs` (maps to WASI). `sys.io.File.saveContent`/`getContent` work. WASM runner grants filesystem access via preopened directories.\n\nEmbedded wasmtime execution. `rayzor run --wasm hello.hx` compiles + links + runs in one command. WASI P1 imports (stdio, env, filesystem). No external wasmtime install needed.\n\n\nJS glue + HTML harness generation. `rayzor build --target wasm --browser`. Canvas/WebGL interop for GPU rendering in browser.\n\nWIT generation from extern class signatures. `EntryKind::WasmComponent` in rpkg format. Loader falls back to WASM component when no native lib for current platform.\n\nFiber runtime: stackless coroutines via CPS transform at MIR level. Same Haxe API (`Future.create`, `.await()`, `.then()`) works on both native (threads) and WASM (cooperative scheduling). Browser: Web Workers + SharedArrayBuffer for parallelism.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_wasm_roadmap` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}